b-p2 = prose (cons "*Hyperactivity* is an ordinary English word for unusually intense activity. Here it also names the continuing activity of constructing, interpreting, and acting on relations. A question can become a computation; an equivalence can carry a construction into another representation; an interaction can make a definition, observation, or proof available for further use. The formal language developed in this paper makes that activity programmable, including the descriptions and interpretations through which participants recognize and use relations. The activity is not bounded by one language implementation, machine, or participant." nil)
